policy_description:
&quot;the Agrarian Law is responsible for regulating land ownership and user rights. According to this law, there are 3 types of lands: agriculture, livestock or forestry lands, and does not recognizes lands dedicated to conservation, an aspect that could enter into conflicts with the General Law for Sustainable Forest Development and with the REDD+ mechanisms. This act also establishes certain restrictions to companies in the forestry sector.&quot;
Last reformed in 2023:
&quot;The Federal Executive will promote the integral and equitable development of the rural sector through the promotion of productive activities and social actions with a gender perspective, aimed at increasing the well-being of the population and their participation in national life, in conditions of equality and parity&quot;.

