policy_description:
The Three Year Action Agenda 2017-18 to 2019-20 &quot;recognizes the goal of decarbonization, and promotes it mainly through productivity and efficiency increases in the economy and renewable energy production. It emphasises the role for government intervention to promote energy efficiency when this can be justified based on cost-benefit analysis. Decarbonization is hence regarded as an important co-benefit of cleaner and more efficient economic growth&quot;
Objectives of the Agenda include:
100 GW Renewable energy capacity by 2019-20, 175 GW by 2022;
Off-grid solar energy capacity of 20 GW by 2019-20, 40 GW by 2022;
Implementation of Renewable Purchase Obligations (RPOs) by 2019-20.
(source: IEA)

